#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# differential_initial

#% text
# `differential_initial(p, u, x)` gives the initial of the differential polynomial `p` in the functions `u` of `x`: the coefficient of the highest power of its leader.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The ranking is `ranking: orderly` (the default) or `ranking: elimination`, as for `differential_leader`. A polynomial without derivatives of the functions is its own initial.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
differential_initial(x*y(x)*y'(x)^2 + y(x)^3, y, x)
#% output
#= x*y(x)

#% cell
differential_initial(derivative(0, 1)(u)(x, t)*derivative(1, 0)(u)(x, t) + u(x, t), u, [x, t])
#% output
#= derivative(0, 1)(u)(x, t)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `differential_leader`, `differential_separant`
